REGEDIT4

; 64-bit Wine's prefixes' session, after wine32-session.reg (wine64-dist.sh
; applies both with reg-apply.py):
;
; - No winemenubuilder from RunServices: wineboot --init started it in
;   every session, a process of its own beside the services, for menu
;   entries no page has. 32-bit Wine's dist has no winemenubuilder.exe, so
;   its sessions never ran one.
; - MountMgr starts at boot again (wine32-session.reg makes it
;   demand-start): 64-bit Wine has its Unix side, and without it the
;   object namespace has no \??\X: drive links, so GetLogicalDrives is 0
;   in every process. The .NET Framework 4.8 installer then finds no drive
;   to extract to and exits with 0x80004005.

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\RunServices]
"winemenubuilder"=-

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\System\CurrentControlSet\Services\MountMgr]
"Start"=dword:00000002

; No debugger at a crash (AeDebug's Debugger, winedbg --auto, gone): on gex
; the program ends at once and gex reports it (kernelbase's report_crash);
; winedbg's report took seconds, its dialog kept the windows up. WoW64's
; 32-bit view the same (dist.sh's pfs_make, where there is one).
[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\Software\Microsoft\Windows NT\CurrentVersion\AeDebug]
"Debugger"=-
